# ---- Frontend (Vite) ----
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://kmlheefyzhhegxmtaovq.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_9R9LMwYGu14evgtEJd4J3Q_CHhDbQsI
# Local dev only, and enforced as such: src/lib/api.ts reads this behind
# `import.meta.env.DEV`, so a production build collapses to same-origin "/api"
# and cannot pick the value up even if it is set. It points `npm run dev` at the
# uvicorn backend; note that it is a *build-time* value, so before the DEV guard
# a `npm run build` on a laptop with this line baked localhost into the bundle.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
# Error reporting. Leave unset locally — no DSN means the Sentry SDK is never
# initialised, which is how dev, vitest and CI stay out of the issue stream.
# Production's value is committed in .env.production (a browser DSN is public).
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# ---- Backend (FastAPI) ----
ENV=development
# Only honoured where the platform agrees. Vercel sets VERCEL_ENV itself and it
# cannot be overridden from project settings, so on a hosted deployment
# (VERCEL_ENV=production|preview) ENV=development is ignored and production
# wins — the Swagger page, dev CORS and the open DB probe are unreachable there
# regardless of what this says. See config.resolve_env.
#
# Supabase Transaction Pooler (port 6543!) with asyncpg driver.
#
# Connect as `splitdec_app`, not as `postgres`. `postgres` is the project's
# owner role: it owns all eight tables and also carries CREATEROLE, CREATEDB,
# BYPASSRLS, membership in anon/authenticated/service_role, and
# SELECT/UPDATE/DELETE on auth.users, auth.sessions and auth.refresh_tokens.
# `splitdec_app` (20260904100000) holds SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on those
# eight tables, EXECUTE on one wrapper function, and nothing else anywhere --
# which is the entire difference in what a leaked copy of this line is worth.
# tests/test_grants_pg.py asserts that shape against the live database.
#
# The role is created out of band, never in a migration: the statement carries
# a password and supabase/migrations is committed to a public repo. Its
# password is not recoverable from anywhere -- if it is lost, ALTER ROLE a new
# one and update Vercel and this file together.
#
# `postgres` still works and is the rollback for the swap; migrations are still
# applied as `postgres`. Both roles can call public.delete_auth_user, so the
# account-deletion code path does not care which one this names.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://splitdec_app.kmlheefyzhhegxmtaovq:YOUR_DB_PASSWORD@aws-0-eu-west-3.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# Required — there is deliberately no default. It is the trust anchor for every
# token this API accepts, and a forgotten variable used to fall back to the
# production project, so a preview or a fork verified tokens minted by *our*
# Supabase while reading a different database. Its project ref is cross-checked
# against DATABASE_URL's; a mismatch refuses to verify anything.
SUPABASE_URL=https://kmlheefyzhhegxmtaovq.supabase.co
# Legacy HS256 shared secret (Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API -> JWT
# Secret). This project signs with asymmetric keys — its JWKS serves a single
# ES256 key — so HS256 verifies nothing the app issues and is **off unless
# ALLOW_LEGACY_HS256 is set**. Both are needed to turn it back on; the secret
# alone does nothing. Leave both unset unless migrating a project that is still
# on the shared secret.
# ALLOW_LEGACY_HS256=1
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=YOUR_JWT_SECRET
# Required in production for GET /api/health/db (the DB latency probe opens a
# fresh pooler connection per call; without this key the probe returns 503).
HEALTH_PROBE_KEY=GENERATE_A_RANDOM_STRING
# Error reporting for the API function. Unlike the browser DSN this one is not
# public — it is the API's own project — so it lives in Vercel's env, not here.
# Unset locally, so a uvicorn run never reports.
# SENTRY_DSN=

# ---- Auditing (never the app's own connection) ----
# tests/test_grants_pg.py reads catalogs only and is meant to be pointed at
# production — it is the one check that looks at grants as *applied* rather than
# as written in supabase/migrations. Deliberately a different variable from
# TEST_DATABASE_URL, which the write-heavy Postgres tests use and which must
# never name production.
# Keep this one as `postgres`: information_schema.role_table_grants only shows
# a caller the grants it is party to, so auditing as splitdec_app would read
# back a tidier database than the real one.
# AUDIT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://postgres.<ref>:<password>@...:6543/postgres
#
# The write-heavy Postgres tests (test_locks_pg.py, test_balances_pg.py). Point
# it at a throwaway database — a Supabase branch — and **never** production. Use
# the `splitdec_app` credential there rather than `postgres`: those tests are
# the only automated thing that runs the app's real statements as the app's real
# role, so a missing grant shows up as `permission denied` in a test instead of
# in production.
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://splitdec_app.<ref>:<password>@...:6543/postgres

# ---- Build-time only (Vercel Production env), never needed to run the app ----
# Uploads source maps so frontend stack traces are readable instead of minified.
# Without it `npm run build` skips generating maps entirely (vite.config.ts).
# Scope: "Source Map Upload" (project:releases) on the split-dec Sentry org.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
